The nicetime attribute no longer exists in the new API response so there is no nicely formated time for the next cycle. I've used the timestr attribute but it does not include the date.

Hope this is helpful to others.

@txwindsurfer, @sarge31, you're on the right track to fixing the issue. There were significant changes between API v1.3 & v1.4 that broke the Hydrawise component for HA. 

I've already pushed a new Python library [(Hydrawiser v0.2)](https://pypi.org/project/Hydrawiser/) that works again to the v1.4 API. However, to get the HA component fixed will take more effort. A lot has changed in the HA architecture and component integration since I published the component almost 2 years ago. I'm having to refresh myself with HA to get the Hydrawise component integration fixed and and a new pull request issued.

I do plan to fix the Hydrawise component, but it will take me some time.
